> when I try "boot pqa0" or pqb0 or dqa0 or dqb0...

Any device name beginning with a "p" is usually a pseudo-device that
points to the controller itself. The IDE(ATAPI) CD-drives are DQA0
(Delta Quebec Alpha zero) or DQB0 (Delta Quebec Beta zero). Older SRM
consoles might not have been programmed or intended to boot from IDE
devices. SCSI CD drives (DKAnnn) should work fine.

That said, the ARC console (more like a "BIOS") should work for IDE
boot, I believe. 

Perhaps someone with more hands-on experience on your machine will pipe
up. I mostly work with larger Alphas (GS160, GS1280, ES40, ES45, AS4100,
etc.).

