details now.

After my post around 2 AM UTC, I started to dismount the box.

Tilting the PS was tricky, but feasable: The rack is large and heavy, and the
operation is geting especially more difficult because previous admin binded all
wires using many tiraps: all wires are now one big peace of stuff, with legs hanging
the spider every where, so that it come nearly impossible to manipulate the PS as
described on documentations.

After PS were tilt, there are 2 screws at the bottom for each PS: operation of
unscrewing and unpluging cable should be easy, and would be if there were not those
**** tiraps !

NOTE ABOUT 1200 SUPPLIES: the screws used at bottom of supply are NOT the same as
those internal to the box (those that maintain the part of the PS close to the front
of the box)

PS between 1200 ans 4100 are physically very close; dimensions vary of less than
1cm. Still, they do not match exactly, and pinout of plugs do not match at all:
PS are NOT compatible at all between 1200 and 4100.

All my CPUs are ev56 533, so that I could �t those from 4100 into the 1200, and boot
ok. It could be possible to do it reverse way (1200 to 4100) since pinout in EXACTLY
the same, but CPUs on 1200 have bits of plastic added, and I was not to unscrew them
(still, it seemed feasable easily, but I did not want to try that for other reasons:
- was adrk and cold night
- was tired and already had 5h left to remount, tidy up, and sleep before next day
- once that bit of plastic is removed, one have to push VERY HARD to insert the CPU
on the MB ... was already difficult to remove 4100 (deeper cards) CPU from 1200,,
but grabbing a small CPU card from the bottom of a 4100 would surely damage at least
my fingers, and probably expand blood every where, if not damaging some parts of the
computer itself
)

Memory cards have same problem:
- they are exactly compatible at the pinout pouint of view, and plugs are identical;
- 4100 cards are higher, and come out of 1200 box ( but they fit the plug)
- 1200 cards are smaller, can be connected into 4100 but I do not try the challenge
because of probable impossibility to remove it later on.
MEMORY PROBLEM is that my 4100 is using EDO, when my 1200 use extensions for SDRAM:
the 1200 MB do not recognise the 4100 EDO boards, seems to be due to the fact 4100
boards are virtually a single slot each, when the 1200 MB expects extensions for
SDRAM slots (from what I could read on LCD)
=> RAM boards of 4100 fit into 1200, but SRM do not like them  at all.

DIFFERENCES BETWEEN LCDs:
note that order of buttons on LCDs is not identical:
- on 1200 middle is reset, right is halt
- on 4100, middle is halt, right is reset
- ON 4100 THE HALT BUTTON IS NOT PUSH ONCE, BUT TWO STABLE STATE.

The mistake I did about booting, was that halt button was pushed: that induce SRM
never boot the system directly. I dont know if my next problem is due to 4100 or
particular to my SRMv5.5: when I hit 'boot dka5' command, I told yesterday that it
produces immediate reboot. In fact, there was a 1s lag, time for the SRM to record
the parameter in a variable before re-init. When that is done, it does re-init, and
then attempts to boot: whenever I hit boot command, SRM ALWAYS POWER CYCLE THE
SYSTEM BEFORE ACTUALLY BOOTING THE OS.

And since yesterday and days before, the halt button was pulled, any boot always
ended with re-init system, then halt on SRM again. Just had to release that halt
button, then now
>>> boot dka5
does power cycle, but then it really reads my CD and start the OS on the CD.

CPUs:
every thing is fine with 3 CPU. Plug of 4th one is obviously very dirty, what means
to me that the box worked ok for years with that 3 CPU configuration.

About 1200: banks MUST be symetrical between card #0 and card #1, but adjascent slot
may contain diffent sticks. On the other hand, if a pair of slots ( aka a bank) is
compleetely empty, banks of bigger id will be ignored.

btw: I did not try to boot the CD with the faulty supply PLUGGED, and halt button
out. I believe it /should/ boot.

Thats it about the test I did on 4100 and 1200 when trying just to boot a CD with a
falty PS :s

