Unfortunately/annoyingly it would appear that the HP web pages doesn't
include the specs for the 533AU2. Given that the 164LX motherboard can
take the 667 EV56's, I'd be tempted to say that if you can work out the
clock settings / mother board switches you could probably use the 667's.
