> 
> > I was wondering if I can upgrade the processors in my DEC Ultimate
> > Workstation 533AU2. I see Samsung procs fairly often on ebay and I
> > was wondering if I could bump up to a set of 667 or 833 mhz
> > processors. Is there anything higher than 833? What are the L2 cache
> > amounts on the Samsung procs?
> > 
> > If anyone knows, any advice would be appreciated.
> > 
> > Thanks,
> > 
> > Mike
> Unfortunately/annoyingly it would appear that the HP web pages doesn't
> include the specs for the 533AU2. Given that the 164LX motherboard can
> take the 667 EV56's, I'd be tempted to say that if you can work out
> the clock settings / mother board switches you could probably use the
> 667's. The 833's are a different matter as they're sufficiently late
> to be unlikely to be supported by the timer circuits on the mother
> board (although you might be able to hash something up depending on
> your electronics skill level).

Even electronic skills won't help you there. The 833MHz ones are EV68s,
the CPUs employed in the 533AU2 are EV56. Different socket, different
chipset, different anything would be needed. So the only option is to
find a set of (very rare) 667MHz EV56. If an increase of 25% clockwise
is really worth the hassle is doubtful though.
[...]

