Dear Simon,

The Unix installation and filesystem will disappear when you install
Linux if you partition and format the hard drive.  Even if you keep the
existing partitiones you will have to format them, because Linux uses a
different filesystem (ext2 or ext3 vs. UFS).

Or you could get a new hard drive and keep your Unix installation.

As far as CentOS goes, I've never tried it but have heard good things
about it on the redhat_AXP list.

axp-list@redhat.com

good luck

jn



